# Enums in Java



#  What is Enum?

Enum (Enumeration) is a special data type used to represent a fixed set of constants.


#  Why Use Enums?

Instead of using:
String day = "MONDAY";


or:
int status = 1;


we use enums for:

* type safety
* readability
* fixed constants



#  Example

enum Day {
    MONDAY,
    TUESDAY,
    WEDNESDAY
}




#  Important Characteristics

* Enum constants are:

  * public
  * static
  * final

* Enum cannot be instantiated using `new`



#  Syntax
enum Status {
    SUCCESS,
    FAILED,
    PENDING
}




#  Creating Enum Variable

Day today = Day.MONDAY;




#  Enum with switch-case

Enums are heavily used with switch statements.


#  Example

switch(day) {

    case MONDAY:
        System.out.println("Start of week");
        break;
}




#  Enum in if-else

if(day == Day.SUNDAY) {

}




#  Enum Methods

All enums internally extend:
java.lang.Enum
So they get built-in methods.



#  Important Enum Methods

| Method    | Purpose                    |
| ----------------------------------------
| values()  | Returns all constants      |
| ordinal() | Returns index position     |
| name()    | Returns enum constant name |
| valueOf() | Converts String → Enum     |



#  values()

Returns all enum constants as array.
Day.values()




#  ordinal()

Returns index position starting from 0.
Day.MONDAY.ordinal()




#  name()

Returns enum constant name.
Day.FRIDAY.name()



#  valueOf()

Converts string into enum constant.
Day.valueOf("MONDAY")



#  Enum Constructor

Enums can have constructors.


#  Example

enum PizzaSize {

    SMALL(100),
    MEDIUM(200);

    int price;

    PizzaSize(int price) {
        this.price = price;
    }
}




#  Enum with Fields & Methods

Enums can contain:

* variables
* constructors
* methods



#  Advantages of Enums

* Type safety
* Better readability
* Prevent invalid values
* Cleaner switch-case code



#  Real-world Usage

Enums are heavily used in:

* Week days
* Order status
* Payment status
* User roles
* Traffic signals
* API response states
* Spring Boot applications



#  Best Practices

* Use enums for fixed constants
* Prefer enums over String constants
* Use switch-case with enums for cleaner logic



#  Important Interview Point

Enum constructor is always: private
even if not written explicitly.



#  Enum Memory Concept

Enum constants are created only once.

They behave like singleton objects.
